<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis (Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage)",
        "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis faithfully reproduces Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py> ;
    schema:about "Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Explicit Sox9-Bmp-Wnt molecular receptor-ligand kinetics (covered in Slot 017) or Hoxd13 gene dosage polydactyly scaling (covered in Slot 016)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D proximo-distal limb paddle condensation and ECM displacement field plus morphological segmentation of urodele salamander forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] skeletal elements on salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg (r = 0.8744)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with critical traction threshold tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9602 (lambda_c = 6.5435) and 1D spectral-pseudospectral coupled cell-ECM PDE solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5]",
        "reported_in_source: Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod: humerus/femur), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod: radius+ulna / tibia+fibula), and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders)",
        "reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D transverse and 2D proximo-distal limb paddle mechanochemical condensation mapped to urodele salamander 3D skeletal micro-CT reconstructions" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Ambystoma" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py; output: docs/media/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_comparison.png; organism: Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 909c74c2382cbfcf862f8ea9a8529469edfc30728d6d46f34f2904fe31ee564f; artifact_sha256: cae9696ef2245adac8562044612d7f3410d85abb23870b25f25efdbd2d1f2185; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json=fc4767274ebd8ea8..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg=8030c8291c3a6d5b..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/scout_manifest.json=cb9d73c33c4113e4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system | Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod: humerus/femur), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod: radius+ulna / tibia+fibula), and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders); reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with critical traction threshold tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9602 (lambda_c = 6.5435) and 1D spectral-pseudospectral coupled cell-ECM PDE solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] | 2D proximo-distal limb paddle condensation and ECM displacement field plus morphological segmentation of urodele salamander forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] skeletal elements on salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg (r = 0.8744); transfer_boundary: 1D transverse and 2D proximo-distal limb paddle mechanochemical condensation mapped to urodele salamander 3D skeletal micro-CT reconstructions; does_not_claim: Explicit Sox9-Bmp-Wnt molecular receptor-ligand kinetics (covered in Slot 017) or Hoxd13 gene dosage polydactyly scaling (covered in Slot 016)]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4615-6983-1_6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/imammb/1.1.51>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.78.1.83>,
