<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — MorphoEval overall 90.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py` (90.7/100, up from 57.8/100 in Pass 1; +32.9 overall). The remediated implementation integrates the Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM PDE system with biharmonic cell flux regularization and contact-inhibited traction sigma_cell(n) = tau*n^2/(1+lam*n^2), verifying the critical traction bifurcation threshold tau_c = 1.2776 (subcritical tau = 0.85 -> 0 condensations) and exact proximo-distal mode progression [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] (RMSE = 0.0, Pearson r = 1.0000), paired with automated segmentation of the urodele salamander forelimb ([1, 2, 4]: 1 humerus -> 2 ulna/radius -> 4 digits I-IV, spacing 39.00 px, r = 0.8744) and hindlimb ([1, 2, 5]: 1 femur -> 2 tibia/fibula -> 5 digits I-V, spacing 41.50 px) on `salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg`, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_013_mechanochemical_chondrogenesis.lean`. Overall 90.5/100 (faithfulness 90.1, reproducibility 91.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 788718 B, 2352×1400 px, artifact_sha256 cae9696ef2245adac8562044612d7f3410d85abb23870b25f25efdbd2d1f2185 (sha256 cae9696ef2245adac8562044612d7f3410d85abb23870b25f25efdbd2d1f2185), spec_fingerprint 909c74c2382cbfcf862f8ea9a8529469edfc30728d6d46f34f2904fe31ee564f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 909c74c2382cbfcf862f8ea9a8529469edfc30728d6d46f34f2904fe31ee564f; artifact_sha256: cae9696ef2245adac8562044612d7f3410d85abb23870b25f25efdbd2d1f2185; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json=fc4767274ebd8ea8..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg=8030c8291c3a6d5b..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/scout_manifest.json=cb9d73c33c4113e4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system | Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod: humerus/femur), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod: radius+ulna / tibia+fibula), and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders); reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with critical traction threshold tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9602 (lambda_c = 6.5435) and 1D spectral-pseudospectral coupled cell-ECM PDE solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] | 2D proximo-distal limb paddle condensation and ECM displacement field plus morphological segmentation of urodele salamander forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] skeletal elements on salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg (r = 0.8744); transfer_boundary: 1D transverse and 2D proximo-distal limb paddle mechanochemical condensation mapped to urodele salamander 3D skeletal micro-CT reconstructions; does_not_claim: Explicit Sox9-Bmp-Wnt molecular receptor-ligand kinetics (covered in Slot 017) or Hoxd13 gene dosage polydactyly scaling (covered in Slot 016)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D viscoelastic ECM displacement solver to a moving free-boundary apical ectodermal ridge (AER) outgrowth domain.",
        "remediation needed: Hybridize mechanochemical cell traction with Bmp-Sox9-Wnt reaction-diffusion Turing kinetics (Raspopovic et al. 2014, Slot 017) to test mechanochemical-biochemical synergy." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.05e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates 5 proximo-distal mechanochemical regimes across domain width W/lambda_c and traction tau (subcritical tau=0.85 -> m=0, stylopod W=lambda_c -> m=1, zeugopod W=2*lambda_c -> m=2, forelimb autopod W=4*lambda_c -> m=4, hindlimb autopod W=5*lambda_c -> m=5), maps the 2D (W/lambda_c, tau) phase diagram (Panel D), simulates the 2D limb paddle condensation and ECM displacement vector field (Panel C), and exposes CLI flags (`--tau`, `--mode`, `--seed`)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

